ould result in minor flooding across the southern San Juan\nfoothills and communities further downstream.\n\nRivers have responded rapidly to recent rainfall due to saturated\nsoils and increased runoff potential. Thus, prolonged periods of\nadditional rainfall over these regions would trigger a similar\nresponse. The current precipitation forecast suggests larger peaks in\nseveral creeks and rivers than what has been observed over the\nprevious 7 days. However, high end probabilistic rainfall amounts\n(i.e. above 90th percentile) may lead to rivers exceeding action\nstage to minor flooding. Most probable basins to see significant\nrises include; the Rio Blanco, San Juan, Piedra, Los Pinos/Vallecito\nCreek, and the Animas River Basins.\n\nConvective storms and periods of heavy rainfall fed from said\ntropical moisture could result in localized flooding impacts across\nthe CWA, however, confidence decreases rapidly north of the San\nJuans. Please continue to monitor the forecast as these systems\nevolve. Especially for those who reside and/or plan to recreate in\nthe southwest quadrant of the forecast area.","ends":"2026-09-30T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Dolores, CO; Gunnison, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Montezuma, CO; Ouray, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce67801ec73048f07c44dd0418c6a50edd1c8fdc.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce67801ec73048f07c44dd0418c6a50edd1c8fdc.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-26T05:24:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 260524 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1124 PM MDT Fri Sep 25 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Warmer and drier conditions return for the weekend. - Another push of moisture will arrive by Monday, bringing widespread moderate to heavy precipitation through midweek. && .DISCUSSION... Issued at 952 PM MDT Fri Sep 25 2026 PREDOMINATELY DRY THIS WEEKEN","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-25T18:43:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Scattered showers and thunderstorms will be around this afternoon, especially along and south of I-70. Most of eastern Utah and northwest Colorado will remain on the drier side of things. Saturday and Sunday will be mostly dry with a return to unsettled weather next week. Fire weather concerns remain low at this time. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDE","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"lbn01","station_name":"Lebanon","distance_km":5.4,"soil_temp_5cm_f":60.55,"soil_temp_15cm_f":64.58,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":0,"wind_speed_mph":7.78,"air_temp_f":51.69,"relative_humidity":0.795,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/lbn01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KCEZ","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KCEZ 260453Z AUTO 07005KT 10SM CLR 12/11 A3022 RMK AO2 SLP179 T01220106","temp_f":54,"wind_dir":70,"wind_kt":5,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"CLR","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1023.5,"observed":1790398380,"raw_taf":null,"url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KCEZ&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":{"aqi":20,"category":"Good","parameter":"O3","reporting_area":"Four Corners Area","observed":"2026-09-25 22","by_parameter":{"O3":{"aqi":20,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Four Corners Area","observed":"2026-09-25 22"},"PM2.5":{"aqi":14,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Four Corners Area","observed":"2026-09-25 22"},"PM10":{"aqi":5,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Four Corners Area","observed":"2026-09-25 22"}},"url":"https://www.airnow.gov/","distance_km":11.9},"openmeteo_aq":{"pm25":1.5,"pm10":1.6,"co":110,"no2":5.6,"so2":0,"o3":61,"european_aqi"